  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we write\n\n$$\n3({3}^{5})={3}^{1}\\times {3}^{5}.\n$$\n\nSo our expression can be written as\n\n$$\n{3}^{4}\\times {3}^{1}\\times {3}^{5}.\n$$\n\nTo multiply powers of the same base, we simply add the exponents:\n\n$$\n{3}^{4}\\times {3}^{1}\\times {3}^{5}={3}^{4+1+5}={3}^{10}\n$$",
